 ## Background
-The method originates from single-pass GPU solid voxelization techniques, notably presented in "Single-pass GPU Solid Voxelization and Applications" [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to provide efficient, high-resolution surface normals for dynamic scenes without relying on traditional mesh-based normal data. The approach leverages the fact that a local density field, computed via a small kernel, resembles a signed distance field, allowing gradients to serve as accurate normal estimates [S1, unofficial]. It has been applied in particle system collision detection, solid voxelization of dynamic scenes, and various volume rendering shading pipelines [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
